> 
> Actually, the real issue is sharper: Perfection already has a gate mechanism in §4 that makes questioning unnecessary. Gates carry unresolved parameters into the artifact without requiring an interview at all. So there are two solutions to the under-specification problem—ask, or gate—and the prompt privileges the expensive one while forbidding itself from ever steering toward the cheaper option. That's the genuine incoherence.
